        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Nanjing</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 500 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Historical records attribute the first named urban foundations in the area to the 5th century BCE, Yuecheng and Yecheng, though their locations and dates are debated; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-quan">Sun Quan</a> moved his headquarters to Moling in 211 and built the Stone City, and made it his capital in 229.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze River</a> in the Yangtze River Delta, in the south-western corner of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangsu">Jiangsu</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, with the Qinhuai River running through the main urban area and the Ningzheng Ridge round its north, east and south sides.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Capital of Eastern Wu, the Eastern Jin, the Southern dynasties, the Southern Tang, the early Ming and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a>'s Buddhist monasteries; the Ming city wall and Xiaoling mausoleum; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping</a> capital Tianjing; the Treaty of Nanking; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing-massacre">Nanjing Massacre</a> of 1937–1938</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Nanjing is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangsu">Jiangsu</a> province and a sub-provincial city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, with about 9.4 million people.</span></div>
